From 98120e9b0cadfba168d800897702e1dd85090cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 18:58:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports+configstore: GET list/single + DELETE on
 /api/tenants/{tid}/{governance/virtual-keys,mcp/clients}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirror of patch 0020 for the VK and MCP entity groups so all three
per-tenant POSTs from the prior patches now have ergonomic read/delete
partners. Brings the tenant-scoped admin surface to parity for
providers, VKs, and MCP clients.

configstore additions (delegate-then-verify pattern; no deep cascade
refactor needed):
- ConfigStore.GetVirtualKeysByTenant(ctx, tenantID) lists VKs scoped
  to a tenant via a WHERE clause on the existing
  preloadVirtualKeyBaseRelations query.
- ConfigStore.GetVirtualKeyByIDForTenant(ctx, tenantID, id) calls
  GetVirtualKey and collapses to ErrNotFound when tenant_id mismatches.
- ConfigStore.DeleteVirtualKeyForTenant(ctx, tenantID, id) verifies
  tenant ownership before delegating to the existing DeleteVirtualKey
  transaction (which handles the heavy provider-config + budget +
  rate-limit cascade). Brief TOCTOU window between verify and delete
  is acceptable — worst case the caller sees ErrNotFound from the
  delete step.
- ConfigStore.GetMCPClientByIDForTenant + DeleteMCPClientConfigForTenant
  follow the same delegate-then-verify shape for MCP clients.
- MockConfigStore stubs added.
- Tests cover: GetVirtualKeysByTenant isolation, GetVirtualKeyByIDFor-
  Tenant cross-tenant ErrNotFound, DeleteVirtualKeyForTenant only-own-
  tenant, plus the MCP equivalents.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantVirtualKeyHandler gains listVirtualKeys (GET list),
  getVirtualKey (GET single), deleteVirtualKey (DELETE with Evict).
- handlers.TenantMCPHandler gains listMCPClients (GET list),
  getMCPClient (GET single), deleteMCPClient (DELETE with Evict).
- All routes mount under the same RequireTenantPathMiddleware chain
  the POST handlers already use; server.go wiring unchanged.

Layer 1 integration test extended with a Phase 5 — exercise list-by-
tenant for both entity groups (asserts only the calling tenant's rows
come back), DELETE the MCP client for acme + confirm globex's MCP
survives, and a cross-tenant DELETE probe at the store layer that
locks in the ErrNotFound response (the load-bearing safety check).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
